From 6b9f0b294e5effa6329c359fa6ce6954c944d237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WilbertACDX <115293547+WilbertACDX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:43:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] WifiAP: follow the DS's channel instead of sitting on
 channel 6

The emulated access point pinned itself to channel 6 and dropped every
frame the DS sent from any other one, faithfully imitating a radio it
doesn't have. The DS's receive path drops frames tagged with a channel
it isn't tuned to, so to any game whose site survey doesn't happen to
visit 6, melonAP simply does not exist.

Pokemon Black scans channels 1, 7 and 13 -- measured on device: 532/532/531
visits, zero to channel 6, and 611 consecutive frames rejected as "bad
channel 6". The DS never associated and Mystery Gift hung on "searching
for gift" indefinitely. Pokemon SoulSilver worked only because its scan
does reach 6.

There is no radio here, so follow the DS: every frame it sends carries
the channel it sent it on, and replies (and the next beacon) go back out
tagged to match. A game that does tune to 6 behaves exactly as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/WifiAP.cpp | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 src/WifiAP.h   |  6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/WifiAP.cpp b/src/WifiAP.cpp
index 6001da1..b208a0e 100644
--- a/src/WifiAP.cpp
+++ b/src/WifiAP.cpp
@@ -35,7 +35,6 @@ using Platform::LogLevel;
 
